**The bug:**

```java
@Entity
public class Order {
    @Id @GeneratedValue Long id;
    @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY) Customer customer;
    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "order", fetch = FetchType.LAZY) List<OrderItem> items;
}

@RestController
public class OrderController {
    @GetMapping("/orders")
    public List<OrderSummary> list() {
        return orderRepo.findAll().stream()           // 1 SQL
            .map(o -> new OrderSummary(
                o.getId(),
                o.getCustomer().getName(),            // +N SQL (customer)
                o.getItems().size()))                 // +N SQL (items)
            .toList();
    }
}
```

For 100 orders: **201 queries.**

**Measure it in a test so it never regresses:**

```java
@DataJpaTest
@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = NONE)
class OrderQueryCountTest {
    @Autowired EntityManagerFactory emf;
    @Autowired OrderRepository orderRepo;

    @Test
    void findAllOrdersWithCustomer_usesOneQuery() {
        Statistics stats = emf.unwrap(SessionFactory.class).getStatistics();
        stats.setStatisticsEnabled(true);
        stats.clear();

        orderRepo.findAllWithCustomer();

        assertThat(stats.getPrepareStatementCount()).isLessThanOrEqualTo(2);
    }
}
```

**Fix 1 — `@EntityGraph` for the detail/summary:**

```java
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {
    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"customer"})
    List<Order> findAllWithCustomer();

    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"customer", "items"})
    Optional<Order> findById(Long id);
}
```

**Fix 2 — `@BatchSize` for paginated list views:**

```java
@Entity
public class Order {
    @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
    @BatchSize(size = 50)
    Customer customer;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "order", fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
    @BatchSize(size = 50)
    List<OrderItem> items;
}
```

Now `orderRepo.findAll(PageRequest.of(0, 100))` fires **3 queries**: 1 for orders page, 1 batched customer fetch, 1 batched items fetch.

**Fix 3 — DTO projection for a read-only list endpoint:**

```java
public record OrderSummary(Long id, String customerName, long itemCount) {}

@Query("""
    SELECT new com.acme.OrderSummary(o.id, o.customer.name, SIZE(o.items))
    FROM Order o
    ORDER BY o.createdAt DESC
""")
Page<OrderSummary> summaries(Pageable pageable);
```

One query, no entity loading, no lazy proxies, no N+1 possible.

**Pattern 1 — Named graph with subgraph:**

```java
@Entity
@NamedEntityGraph(
    name = "Order.detail",
    attributeNodes = {
        @NamedAttributeNode("customer"),
        @NamedAttributeNode(value = "items", subgraph = "Order.itemsSubgraph")
    },
    subgraphs = {
        @NamedSubgraph(
            name = "Order.itemsSubgraph",
            attributeNodes = @NamedAttributeNode("product"))
    }
)
public class Order { ... }

public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {
    @EntityGraph(value = "Order.detail", type = EntityGraph.EntityGraphType.FETCH)
    Optional<Order> findDetailById(Long id);
}
```

One JPQL query, one SQL with nested LEFT JOINs. Perfect for an order-detail endpoint.

**Pattern 2 — ID-first pagination for list views with collections:**

```java
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {
    @Query("SELECT o.id FROM Order o WHERE o.status = :status ORDER BY o.createdAt DESC")
    Page<Long> findIdsByStatus(@Param("status") OrderStatus status, Pageable page);

    @EntityGraph(attributePaths = {"items"})
    List<Order> findByIdIn(Collection<Long> ids);
}

@Service
class OrderQueryService {
    public Page<Order> listWithItems(OrderStatus status, Pageable page) {
        Page<Long> idPage = orderRepo.findIdsByStatus(status, page);
        List<Order> orders = orderRepo.findByIdIn(idPage.getContent());
        Map<Long, Order> byId = orders.stream()
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(Order::getId, Function.identity()));
        List<Order> ordered = idPage.getContent().stream().map(byId::get).toList();
        return new PageImpl<>(ordered, page, idPage.getTotalElements());
    }
}
```

ID query paginates correctly (no JOIN). Entity query eagerly loads items with no pagination (no Cartesian).

**Pattern 3 — Dynamic graph at runtime:**

```java
@Service
class OrderQueryService {
    @PersistenceContext EntityManager em;

    public Optional<Order> findWithDynamicGraph(Long id, Set<String> includes) {
        EntityGraph<Order> graph = em.createEntityGraph(Order.class);
        if (includes.contains("customer")) graph.addAttributeNodes("customer");
        if (includes.contains("items"))    graph.addAttributeNodes("items");
        if (includes.contains("payments")) graph.addAttributeNodes("payments");

        TypedQuery<Order> q = em.createQuery(
            "SELECT o FROM Order o WHERE o.id = :id", Order.class);
        q.setParameter("id", id);
        q.setHint("jakarta.persistence.fetchgraph", graph);
        return q.getResultList().stream().findFirst();
    }
}
```

Lets the caller request `GET /orders/42?include=customer,items` — Hibernate generates exactly the joins needed.
